    (8::int, 'Which of the following is the original source of all new alleles (gene versions)?'::text, NULL::text, 'Predation'::text, 'Mutations'::text, 'Fossilization'::text, 'Migration of birds'::text, 'B'::text, 'Adaptation and Variation'::text, 'hard'::text),
    (8::int, 'The color change of the peppered moth during the Industrial Revolution demonstrated that ___.'::text, 'diagram://peppered'::text, 'moths paint themselves darker'::text, 'predators stopped eating moths'::text, 'natural selection can change the frequency of traits in a population'::text, 'soot enters cells and changes color directly'::text, 'C'::text, 'Natural Selection'::text, 'medium'::text),
    (8::int, 'Scientists reconstruct the appearance and behavior of long-extinct organisms mainly using ___.'::text, 'diagram://fossil'::text, 'fossil evidence'::text, 'weather records'::text, 'modern maps'::text, 'leaves of plants'::text, 'A'::text, 'Fossil Evidence'::text, 'medium'::text),
    (8::int, 'Human wisdom teeth are sometimes considered vestigial because ___.'::text, NULL::text, 'they grow only in adults above 60'::text, 'they never develop in anyone'::text, 'they are less needed today because our diet and cooking changed'::text, 'they are the same as the appendix'::text, 'C'::text, 'Vestigial Structures'::text, 'medium'::text),
    (8::int, 'When two species share many similar genes and similar developmental stages, it strongly suggests they ___.'::text, 'diagram://embryo'::text, 'evolved from a relatively recent common ancestor'::text, 'appeared at the same time with no connection'::text, 'are identical species'::text, 'evolved completely separately'::text, 'A'::text, 'Common Ancestry'::text, 'medium'::text),
    (9::int, 'Mosquitoes became resistant to the pesticide DDT after decades of spraying. This happened because ___.'::text, NULL::text, 'the chemical changed their DNA multiple times in one generation'::text, 'DDT created brand-new resistance genes in every mosquito'::text, 'mosquitoes learned to avoid the chemical'::text, 'resistance alleles increased in frequency through natural selection'::text, 'D'::text, 'Natural Selection'::text, 'hard'::text),
    (9::int, 'Why do doctors advise patients to finish a full course of antibiotics?'::text, NULL::text, 'To prevent the infection from becoming viral'::text, 'To reduce the chance that resistant bacteria survive and spread'::text, 'To make the antibiotics more colorful'::text, 'To help bacteria grow faster'::text, 'B'::text, 'Natural Selection'::text, 'medium'::text),
    (9::int, 'Transitional fossils such as Tiktaalik provide evidence of ___.'::text, 'diagram://fossil'::text, 'fossils forming in living tissue'::text, 'the sudden appearance of complex life'::text, 'evolution from fish-like ancestors to land vertebrates'::text, 'species never changing'::text, 'C'::text, 'Fossil Evidence'::text, 'medium'::text),
    (9::int, 'Scientists use DNA comparisons to trace how viruses spread because ___.'::text, 'diagram://dna'::text, 'viruses cannot mutate'::text, 'DNA tells us the virus color'::text, 'viruses are not made of genetic material'::text, 'mutations accumulate at a measurable rate (molecular clock)'::text, 'D'::text, 'Evidence of Evolution'::text, 'medium'::text),
    (9::int, 'Species X shares 95% of its DNA with species P and only 85% with species Q. Based on this evidence, ___.'::text, NULL::text, 'Q and P are the same species'::text, 'DNA cannot be used for relationships'::text, 'species X is more closely related to Q than to P'::text, 'species X is more closely related to P than to Q'::text, 'D'::text, 'Evidence of Evolution'::text, 'medium'::text),
    (9::int, 'Similar developmental "master control" genes (such as Hox genes) found in both flies and humans indicate ___.'::text, 'diagram://embryo'::text, 'no evolutionary relationship at all'::text, 'a common ancestor that lived very long ago'::text, 'that the genes formed by coincidence in each species'::text, 'that flies evolved from humans'::text, 'B'::text, 'Evidence of Evolution'::text, 'hard'::text),
    (9::int, 'Some cave-dwelling animals have eyes that cannot see or no eyes at all. Their eyes are considered ___.'::text, NULL::text, 'fossil fuels'::text, 'vestigial structures'::text, 'reproductive organs'::text, 'analogous structures'::text, 'B'::text, 'Vestigial Structures'::text, 'medium'::text),
    (9::int, 'A camel''s hump (fat store) and broad feet are adaptations for living in ___.'::text, NULL::text, 'deserts'::text, 'coral reefs'::text, 'rainforests'::text, 'tundra'::text, 'A'::text, 'Adaptation and Variation'::text, 'medium'::text),
    (9::int, 'The closer two species are located on a phylogenetic tree, the more recently ___.'::text, 'diagram://tree'::text, 'fossils formed between them'::text, 'they became extinct'::text, 'they developed identical DNA'::text, 'they shared a common ancestor'::text, 'D'::text, 'Phylogenetic Trees'::text, 'hard'::text),
    (9::int, 'All organisms share the same basic biochemistry - ATP for energy, DNA for heredity, and ribosomes for protein synthesis. This strongly suggests ___.'::text, NULL::text, 'that biochemistry is irrelevant to evolution'::text, 'a single common origin of life'::text, 'many completely independent origins of life'::text, 'that life started only recently'::text, 'B'::text, 'Common Ancestry'::text, 'hard'::text),
    (10::int, 'Which modern technique provides the most precise evidence for how closely related two species are?'::text, 'diagram://dna'::text, 'Just looking at their colors'::text, 'Comparing their DNA sequences'::text, 'Observing them for one day'::text, 'Counting their limbs only'::text, 'B'::text, 'Evidence of Evolution'::text, 'medium'::text),
    (10::int, 'The popular term "missing link" best refers to ___.'::text, 'diagram://fossil'::text, 'a rock layer without fossils'::text, 'a fossil with no bones'::text, 'a species that cannot evolve'::text, 'transitional fossil forms that show intermediate traits between major groups'::text, 'D'::text, 'Fossil Evidence'::text, 'hard'::text),
    (10::int, 'The bones in a horse leg, dolphin flipper, and bat wing are homologous because they ___.'::text, 'diagram://homologous'::text, 'evolved independently with the same function'::text, 'are identical in shape and function'::text, 'share a common evolutionary origin despite different functions'::text, 'are all made of cartilage only'::text, 'C'::text, 'Homologous Structures'::text, 'medium'::text),
    (10::int, 'The tail fin of a fish and the flukes of a whale have a similar shape for swimming, but they did not come from a common ancestor with that trait. They are ___.'::text, 'diagram://analogous'::text, 'fossil structures'::text, 'vestigial structures'::text, 'homologous structures'::text, 'analogous structures'::text, 'D'::text, 'Analogous Structures'::text, 'medium'::text),
    (10::int, 'The study of industrial melanism in peppered moths clearly demonstrated natural selection because ___.'::text, 'diagram://peppered'::text, 'birds stopped reproducing'::text, 'moths were painted by humans'::text, 'researchers measured allele frequency changes of a heritable trait when the environment changed'::text, 'soot changed the moths'' DNA instantly'::text, 'C'::text, 'Natural Selection'::text, 'hard'::text),
    (10::int, 'When a phylogenetic tree built from DNA data and another built from fossil data independently agree, this ___.'::text, 'diagram://tree'::text, 'proves the methods are wrong'::text, 'strengthens confidence in the inferred evolutionary relationships'::text, 'weakens the evidence for common descent'::text, 'shows fossils are unnecessary'::text, 'B'::text, 'Phylogenetic Trees'::text, 'hard'::text),
    (10::int, 'Using a cladogram where A, B, and C share ancestor X, and B and C share an additional recent ancestor Y, which statement is true?'::text, 'diagram://cladogram'::text, 'B and C share no traits'::text, 'A and C are more closely related than B and C'::text, 'B and C are more closely related to each other than either is to A'::text, 'A, B, and C are equally related'::text, 'C'::text, 'Cladograms'::text, 'hard'::text),
    (10::int, 'The universal genetic code shared by all living things is powerful evidence for ___.'::text, NULL::text, 'evolution having stopped'::text, 'life starting several times without connection'::text, 'a common ancestor for all life'::text, 'many unrelated origins of life'::text, 'C'::text, 'Common Ancestry'::text, 'medium'::text),
    (10::int, 'The gradual change in the traits of a population over many generations is known as ___.'::text, NULL::text, 'evolution'::text, 'erosion'::text, 'condensation'::text, 'weathering'::text, 'A'::text, 'Adaptation and Variation'::text, 'medium'::text),
    (10::int, 'Why do harmless vestigial structures often remain in populations for millions of years?'::text, NULL::text, 'Organisms actively maintain them for decoration'::text, 'They are always deadly and still persist'::text, 'Natural selection does not remove them because they cause little or no harm and are inherited leftovers'::text, 'Fossils prevent them from disappearing'::text, 'C'::text, 'Vestigial Structures'::text, 'medium'::text)
  ) as v(level_number, question_text, image_url, choice_a, choice_b, choice_c, choice_d,
         correct_answer, topic, difficulty)
  on l.level_number = v.level_number;
